{"entryId":"3214","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3214:1","sourceSha256":"135e0ba2f258fc0953c0e0bb7f8630b63be8e50651fec65a344f8a4a57f782da","englishSha256":"da4d3ac42b9f7930f389de96bf54627845bd7da5154c9e0734781dabb478413c","citations":[{"id":"3214:1:link-001","he":[13,47],"en":[18,57],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_63a.2"},"reference":"Eruvin 63a:2","assessment":"Ravina explicitly calls himself Rav Ashi’s talmid haver.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 63a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_63a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Eruvin 63a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_63a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-002","he":[49,103],"en":[58,155],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.6"},"reference":"Beitzah 6a:6","assessment":"The dialogue is about setting aside an eruv, not taking a seat. Both the checked Bavli and Shittah print Assi in the lemma; Rashi and the Shittah’s discussion identify Ashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 6a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Beitzah 6a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Beitzah 6a:6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Beitzah_6a.6.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-003","he":[105,157],"en":[156,244],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_6a.4"},"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 6a:4","assessment":"The Shittah makes exactly that argument and cites Eruvin.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 6a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_6a.4"},"witness":"Vilna Ed"},{"reference":"Eruvin 63a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_63a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-004","he":[159,193],"en":[245,289],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Yoma_86a.10.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Yoma 86a:10:1","assessment":"Rashi explicitly glosses Mata Mehasya as Ravina’s locale.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Yoma 86a:10:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Yoma_86a.10.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-005","he":[194,227],"en":[290,345],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.103"},"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:103","assessment":"Sherira explicitly gives Rav Ashi’s position in Mata Mehasya. The Rashi locus concerns Ravina.","evidence":[{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:103","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.103"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-006","he":[229,350],"en":[346,594],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.1"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:1","assessment":"The checked Bavli directly gives the end-of-teaching formula and the verse as mnemonic. Heilprin’s verbal associations explain the separate cues.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-007","he":[393,434],"en":[671,684],"target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/halichot-olam/halichot-olam01.pdf#page=11"},"reference":"Halikhot Olam, Gate I, chapter 2, p. 11","assessment":"The checked Halikhot Olam and London Yuhasin both give the mnemonic. The Bavli already connects the verse to the end-of-teaching formula.","evidence":[{"reference":"Halikhot Olam, Gate I, chapter 2, p. 11","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/halichot-olam/halichot-olam01.pdf#page=11"},"witness":"Halikhot Olam, Gate I, chapter 2, p. 11"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 187","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=43"},"witness":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 187"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-008","he":[393,434],"en":[689,714],"target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=43"},"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 187","assessment":"The checked Halikhot Olam and London Yuhasin both give the mnemonic. The Bavli already connects the verse to the end-of-teaching formula.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 187","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=43"},"witness":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 187"},{"reference":"Halikhot Olam, Gate I, chapter 2, p. 11","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/halichot-olam/halichot-olam01.pdf#page=11"},"witness":"Halikhot Olam, Gate I, chapter 2, p. 11"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-009","he":[436,468],"en":[747,805],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.2"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:2","assessment":"The mnemonic is explicitly the Bavli’s. The charge of forgetting belongs to Heilprin’s polemic and remains attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 86a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_86a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-010","he":[470,612],"en":[1056,1075],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","assessment":"The checked Epistle and Part I 4234 give Wednesday, while this dossier gives Sunday. Part I 4181 reports a different death year and Part I 4259 repeats the date corresponding to Seleucid 811.","evidence":[{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27קפא&oldid=470701"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רנט&oldid=470722"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-011","he":[470,612],"en":[896,903],"target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רנט&oldid=470722"},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259","assessment":"The checked Epistle and Part I 4234 give Wednesday, while this dossier gives Sunday. Part I 4181 reports a different death year and Part I 4259 repeats the date corresponding to Seleucid 811.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רנט&oldid=470722"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259"},{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27קפא&oldid=470701"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-012","he":[470,612],"en":[930,934],"target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27קפא&oldid=470701"},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181","assessment":"The checked Epistle and Part I 4234 give Wednesday, while this dossier gives Sunday. Part I 4181 reports a different death year and Part I 4259 repeats the date corresponding to Seleucid 811.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27קפא&oldid=470701"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181"},{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רנט&oldid=470722"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-013","he":[470,612],"en":[939,953],"target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","assessment":"The checked Epistle and Part I 4234 give Wednesday, while this dossier gives Sunday. Part I 4181 reports a different death year and Part I 4259 repeats the date corresponding to Seleucid 811.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"},{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27קפא&oldid=470701"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4181"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רנט&oldid=470722"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4259"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-014","he":[614,644],"en":[1208,1218],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Makkot_10a.21"},"reference":"Makkot 10a:21","assessment":"The dossier has “to learn.” Makkot assigns learning to Rav Ashi and teaching to Ravina, a distinction Heilprin himself discusses in the Introduction.","evidence":[{"reference":"Makkot 10a:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Makkot_10a.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Makkot 10a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Makkot_10a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Introduction:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Seder_HaDorot%2C_Introduction.28"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1878-1882"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-015","he":[646,703],"en":[1311,1329],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Seder_HaDorot%2C_Introduction.28"},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Introduction:28","assessment":"The Introduction explicitly reads Ravina’s saying as teaching, then considers Maharsha’s view that Ashi was older and argues the reverse for the pupil-colleague. The identifications are attributed arguments.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Introduction:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Seder_HaDorot%2C_Introduction.28"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1878-1882"},{"reference":"Chidushei Agadot on Bava Metzia 86a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chidushei_Agadot_on_Bava_Metzia_86a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-016","he":[705,761],"en":[1393,1496],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_39b.2"},"reference":"Berakhot 39b:2","assessment":"The source directly supplies the father tradition through Ravina’s mother.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 39b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_39b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-017","he":[763,809],"en":[1497,1612],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_68b.10"},"reference":"Menachot 68b:10","assessment":"The fuller source specifies the evening after the seventeenth leading into the eighteenth. It again attributes the report to Ravina’s mother.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 68b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_68b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-018","he":[836,878],"en":[1649,1665],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_60b.3"},"reference":"Nedarim 60b:3","assessment":"Both Nedarim occurrences have Marimar reporting Ravina’s father. The checked 60b brackets Yosef and 90a gives Pappi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 60b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_60b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 90a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_90a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2551:1","target":{"entry":2551,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-019","he":[836,878],"en":[1670,1686],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_90a.8"},"reference":"Nedarim 90a:8","assessment":"Both Nedarim occurrences have Marimar reporting Ravina’s father. The checked 60b brackets Yosef and 90a gives Pappi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 90a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_90a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 60b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_60b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2551:1","target":{"entry":2551,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-020","he":[836,878],"en":[1692,1699],"target":{"entry":2551,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 2551:1","assessment":"Both Nedarim occurrences have Marimar reporting Ravina’s father. The checked 60b brackets Yosef and 90a gives Pappi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2551:1","target":{"entry":2551,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Nedarim 60b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_60b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 90a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_90a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-021","he":[880,934],"en":[1702,1839],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_66a.23"},"reference":"Niddah 66a:23","assessment":"Niddah gives the match and subsequent challenge as distinct turns in the story. The named Hanina notice cites the same occurrence.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 66a:23","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_66a.23"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Niddah 66a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_66a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1478:1","target":{"entry":1478,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-022","he":[936,1059],"en":[1840,2017],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.6"},"reference":"Beitzah 6a:6","assessment":"The checked Bavli preserves Assi parenthetically. Rashi explicitly identifies the one Ravina saw as Rav Ashi. The next segment directly quotes the Rava statement.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 6a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Beitzah 6a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_6a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Beitzah 6a:6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Beitzah_6a.6.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-023","he":[1061,1179],"en":[2018,2268],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_24b.6"},"reference":"Berakhot 24b:6","assessment":"The exact episode is Berakhot 24b:6. The checked witness has Rav Yehudah, a plausible alternate expansion of the raw abbreviation. Rav Ashi asks and Ravina answers.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 24b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_24b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-024","he":[1181,1239],"en":[2269,2384],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_109a.5"},"reference":"Shabbat 109a:5","assessment":"The checked alternate narratives quote Rav Hillel and Rava respectively and accompany distinct treatments. The two chains remain separate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 109a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_109a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 109a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_109a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3214:1:link-025","he":[1241,1320],"en":[2385,2511],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.3"},"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:3","assessment":"The Bavli has Ravina’s death and Rav Ashi asking Bar Kippok about the occasion, which Rashi identifies as the day of death. Sherira’s final Ravina is placed after Rav Ashi; the identification and chronology stay unresolved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Moed Katan 25b:4:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Moed_Katan_25b.4.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,8,9,13,14,15,16,17,20,21,22,23,24],"holds":[{"raw":"ובצמח דוד ד\"א רל\"ד כתב רבינא סוף אמוראים","reason":"Heilprin’s Part I supplies a related quotation and chronology. A directly checked Tzemah David witness of this full attribution remains pending.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"}]},{"raw":"וע\"ש אי רב אשי קשיש מיניה או להיפך","reason":"Heilprin argues that Ravina was older. Maharsha argues that Rav Ashi was older. The age question remains attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Introduction:28","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Seder_HaDorot%2C_Introduction.28"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1878-1882"},{"reference":"Chidushei Agadot on Bava Metzia 86a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chidushei_Agadot_on_Bava_Metzia_86a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"כתב היוחסין אבוי דרבינא","reason":"The adjacent Nedarim parallels name the father only as your father. The exact Yuhasin father-entry citation remains uncollated.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 60b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_60b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 90a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_90a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ומת קודם רב אשי","reason":"The eulogy is directly attested for a Ravina. Sherira’s dated notice of Avina son of Rav Huna belongs to a chronology after Rav Ashi. Whether both witnesses refer to the same Ravina remains unresolved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Moed Katan 25b:4:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Moed_Katan_25b.4.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Epistle of Rav Sherira Gaon 1:108","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Epistle_of_Rav_Sherira_Gaon_1.108"},"witness":"Seder HaChachamim. Oxford, 1888"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234","target":{"url":"https://wiki.jewishbooks.org.il/mediawiki/index.php?title=סדר_הדורות/א/ד%27רלד&oldid=470716"},"witness":"Seder HaDorot, Part I, AM 4234"}]},{"raw":"הלכה כמותו נגד רב אחא ורב אשי (ע\"ש)","reason":"Hullin 93b gives a rule with three exceptions for Rav Aha and Ravina. The combined rule against both Rav Aha and Rav Ashi is not established by that locus.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 93b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_93b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The dossier calls Ravina the Later a pupil-colleague. Heilprin’s Introduction and Maharsha disagree about relative age. The Epistle chronology and the eulogy leave the identity open.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"This dossier gives Sunday, 13 Kislev. The checked Epistle and Heilprin’s Part I for AM 4234 give Wednesday. Part I AM 4181 and AM 4259 report different death years.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Th